WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.013
- [Narrator] In France,
pastry reigns supreme.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.290
From the kouign-amann,
to the pain au chocolat,

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.588
it's all here.

00:00:07.588 --> 00:00:08.467
- (in foreign language)

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:09.747
- (in foreign language)

00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:11.590
(laughs)

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.090
- Wait what is happening here?

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.223
(cheerful music)

00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:19.440
So, it turns out that the
name of this pastry has

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.700
been at the center of a debate in France

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.910
for quite some time now.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.937
The question at hand:
"What do you call this?"

00:00:27.937 --> 00:00:28.770
- (in foreign language)

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.770
- (in foreign language)

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.210
- There seem to be two camps.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.227
Those that call this:

00:00:33.227 --> 00:00:34.156
- (in foreign language)

00:00:34.156 --> 00:00:35.087
- And those that call it:

00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:36.490
- (in foreign language)

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:37.700
- And according to this map,

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.460
it's clear where the
lines have been drawn.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.660
So, here we are, in
France, not to pick a side,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.730
but to hear from both camps.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.533
We begin in Paris, with
the pain au chocolat.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:55.576
- (in foreign language)

